      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gmail-watcher): catch renewal interval errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Gmail watcher sets up a `setInterval` that calls `startGmailWatch(runtimeConfig)` as a fire-and-forget `void` expression. If the periodic Gmail API watch registration fails, the rejection becomes an unhandled rejection and can crash the gateway process hours after startup.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a `.catch` to the renewal `startGmailWatch` call. On rejection, a warning is logged and the watcher keeps running, so the next renewal cycle can retry. The initial startup path is unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong-running gateways with the Gmail hook enabled no longer crash on transient Gmail API renewal failures.\n\n## Evidence\n\nTerminal proof (after fix):\n\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/gmail-watcher-renewal-catch.mts\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n=== Proof: gmail-watcher renewal interval rejection catch ===\n\nRunning focused regression test: catches renewal interval errors instead of letting them become unhandled rejections\n\n... (vitest output) ...\n\nPASS: renewal interval rejection is caught and does not become unhandled.\n```\n\nRegression test:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/hooks/gmail-watcher.test.ts\n```\n\nAll 9 tests pass.\n",
        "branch": "fix/gmail-watcher-renewal-catch",
